{%- comment -%}
  Single source of truth for the 9 games, so the header's game selector
  and the home/all-games game grid don't each need manual theme-editor
  configuration to work. Real collection data (title, url, product count,
  featured_image) is pulled live via `collections['{slug}']` wherever this
  is used — this registry only supplies what Shopify collections don't
  carry: the card gradient and a fallback icon for before a merchant
  uploads a real collection image.

  Icon/thumbnail URLs are bloxcart.com's own live marketing assets
  (media.bloxcart.com/payload-media/, a Payload CMS bucket separate from
  the Shopify product catalog — confirmed via the site's own homepage
  <link rel=preload> tags, see docs/catalog-audit.md). They're hotlinked
  here as a stopgap; swap in `collection.image` once one is uploaded per
  collection in Shopify Admin and this fallback stops being used.

  Adopt Me is the one confirmed external-only entry (no internal catalog,
  real NeonPets affiliate link) — see PHASE_0_EXTRACTION_NOTES.md.

  Usage:
    {%- capture games_json -%}{% render 'game-registry' %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign games = games_json | parse_json -%}
    {%- for game in games -%} ... {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
